// TWO offenders and TWO reports under one "Formula terms" wf header.
//
// HS `prettyWfErrorReport` (Theory/Tools/Wellformedness.hs:118-126) groups the
// report by topic with `groupOn fst`, so a topic's underlined header is printed
// ONCE and its errors follow at `nest 2`, separated by a blank line.  The
// shared closing paragraph ("The only allowed terms are …") belongs to each
// error rather than to the topic, so it repeats per offending formula.  Inside
// one error, `checkTerms` lays the offenders out with `punctuate comma $ map
// (nest 2 . text . quote . show)` under an `fsep`
// (Theory/Tools/Wellformedness.hs:964-966).  Both lemmas below hold reducible
// `em`/`*` terms, and `formulaReports` (Wellformedness.hs:999-1000) walks them
// in theory order:
//
//   - `OneOffenderGround` contributes ONE offender, so its list is a single
//     quoted term with no comma;
//   - `TwoOffendersBound` contributes TWO, which is where the comma and the
//     continuation indent appear.
//
// The offender spelling is HS's `instance Show (Term a)`
// (Term/Term/Raw.hs:227-238), not `prettyTerm`: a builtin AC head prints as
// the `Show ACSym` constructor applied prefix — `Mult(…)`, never infix `*` —
// and commas carry no following space.  The operands are the flattened, sorted
// multiset, and `data FunSym = NoEq … | AC … | C … | List`
// (Term/Term/FunctionSymbols.hs:150-154) ranks `NoEq` before `C`, so `f`/`aaa`
// precede `em` and the source order `em(x, y) * f(x, y)` comes back reversed.
// `em` is a C symbol, whose smart constructor sorts too (`fAppC`,
// Term/Term/Raw.hs:133-134), so `em(x, y)` prints with its arguments in index
// order while the `NoEq` `aaa(x, y)` beside it keeps source order — the two
// halves of one offender disagree on purpose.  The `Bound` indices are counted
// from the innermost binder, and the `Ex #j` around the second offender shifts
// them, so the same source `x`/`y` read `Bound 2`/`Bound 1` in one offender and
// `Bound 3`/`Bound 2` in the other.
//
// The rules keep `*` out of their terms, which keeps this fixture's wf slice
// down to the "Formula terms" topic alone: a rule holding a multiplication
// raises "Multiplication restriction of rules" into the same slice, and that
// report is pinned by mult_restricted_report.spthy.
//
// Compared slices: the wf report block AND the `theory … end` echo (see
// check.sh) — the echo prints the same terms through `prettyTerm` instead, so
// the fixture holds the `Show` spelling and the pretty spelling of one term
// against each other.

theory FormulaTermsOffenders
begin

builtins: bilinear-pairing
functions: f/2, aaa/2

rule R:
  [ Fr(~a), Fr(~b) ] --[ Test(~a), Test2(~b) ]-> [ ]

lemma OneOffenderGround:
  "All #i. Test(em('g', 'h') * f('g', 'h')) @ #i ==> F"

lemma TwoOffendersBound:
  "All x y #i.
     Test2(em(x, y) * aaa(x, y)) @ #i ==> Ex #j. Test(em(x, y) * f(x, y)) @ #j"

end
